Package: network-manager-outline
Architecture: linux-any
Depends:
 network-manager,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Suggests:
 plasma-nm-outline,
Description: NetworkManager VPN plugin for Outline
 Connects to Outline (Shadowsocks) servers with an Outline access key,
 without the Outline client. The tunnel is implemented with outline-sdk and
 managed by NetworkManager like any other VPN: routes, DNS through
 systemd-resolved, and the connection state.
 .
 This package contains the VPN service. Connections can be created with
 nmcli; install plasma-nm-outline for the KDE Plasma settings UI.

Package: plasma-nm-outline
Architecture: linux-any
Depends:
 network-manager-outline (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${plasmanm:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Enhances:
 plasma-nm,
Description: Outline VPN support for the Plasma network applet
 Adds "Outline VPN" to the KDE Plasma network settings and lets the network
 applet connect Outline connections. Access keys can be pasted, imported from
 a text file, stored in KWallet, or asked for on every connect.
 .
 plasma-nm has no stable plugin interface, so this package works only with
 the plasma-nm version it was built against.
